2.3.   Population density
Funafuti is the most densely populated island in Tuvalu, hosting over 60% of the country’s 
population. In comparison to 2017, the population density in Funafuti increased by about 8% 
from 2,399 to 2,590 persons per square-kilometre (Central Statistics Division 2017).
