It should be noted that the land area for Funafuti and the other Islands has decreased over time 
primarily due to soil erosion on the small islets, exacerbated by a cyclone submerging one islet. 
The LiDAR survey compared historical island sizes to their measurements at the time of the 
study in 2019 but did not include the reclaimed lands in Funafuti, as these were added later 
(Government of Tuvalu 2019). 
