3.  Socio-cultural characteristics
3.1.   Household occupants
A household refers to a family or a group of people who usually eat together and share 
resources. There were 1,799 households in 2022, representing an 11% increase from the 2017 
Tuvalu Census. About 55% of the households were enumerated in Funafuti, which is consistent 
with the proportion of the population living on the island. The average household had about 
6 members, similar to the figure published in 2017. However, the average household size in 
Funafuti decreased from 7.4 members in 2017 to 6.7 members in 2022 while it increased in the 
Outer Islands from 4.5 members in 2017 to 5.1 members in 2022.
