3.2.   Religion and ethnicity
About 4 in 5 people in Tuvalu are affiliated with the Ekalesia Kelisiano Tuvalu (EKT) 
religious denomination, making it the largest religious group in the country. The remaining 
denominations account for about 14%, with the Brethren accounting for the next largest 
religious group – at 3%.
