7.  People with disability
7.1.   Method used to collect data on disability
The questionnaire for the Tuvalu 2022 PHC utilised the set of questions from the Washington 
Group on Disability Statistics to gather data on disability. The questions are designed to capture 
various disability domains, such as vision, hearing, self-care, cognition and walking, as well as the 
severity of the disability. The questions, addressed to the population aged 5 years and over, are 
listed below:
1. Does (name) have difficulty in seeing, even if wearing glasses?
2. Does (name) have difficulty in hearing, even if wearing a hearing aid?
3. Does (name) have difficulty in walking or climbing steps?
4. Does (name) have difficulty in remembering or concentrating?
5. Does (name) have difficulty with self-care, such as washing all over and dressing?
6. Does (name) have difficulty communicating using customary language, such as 
understanding or being understood?
The corresponding responses are then recorded in one of the following forms: 
1. No, no difficulty
2. Yes, some difficulty
3. Yes, a lot of difficulty
4. Cannot do at all
The three disability categories that are possible when applying the Washington Group tools are 
outlined below.
