10.2.   Type of living quarters
The most common type of living quarter is the one-family detached house. Compared to the 
Outer Islands, households living in a one-family house attached to one or more houses are 
much more common in Funafuti. Very few households live in apartments, which is expected 
considering there are very few apartment-type dwellings in Tuvalu. Similarly, very few 
households live in shared homes and dwellings attached to non-resident buildings.
