10.3.   Housing structure
Information about the main house construction material was not collected in the Tuvalu 2017 
Mini-PHC; thus, comparing the Tuvalu 2022 PHC to 2017 results is impossible. However, a 
comparison can be made to the Tuvalu 2012 PHC. Concrete is the most common material used 
in main house construction. About half of the houses are made of concrete in Funafuti, and the 
proportion is higher in the Outer Islands (70.2%). On the other hand, timber houses are more 
common in Funafuti (27.7%) compared to the Outer Islands (13.1%).
