10.4.   Energy for cooking and lighting
About 8 out of every 10 households use gas as a source of cooking energy, which is more 
common in Funafuti. There was a significant increase in the proportion of households relying 
on gas as a cooking energy source in the Outer Islands. An increase is observed in the use 
of electricity as a cooking source compared to a decrease in the use of kerosene, wood, and 
coconut parts in the Outer Islands. Except for coconut parts, the same is observed for Funafuti.
