10.5.   Water and sanitation
The main source of drinking water is piped into the dwelling. It is piped from a water storage 
tank/concrete cistern that collects rainwater. Compared to 2017, a higher proportion of 
households now have piped water in their dwellings. Apart from the source “piped into the yard” , 
the same is observed for other sources. There is a significant decrease in water sources piped to 
the yard. A similar result is observed for the main water source for cooking and handwashing.
